## Frontend Quality Checklist

- Test layouts at mobile, tablet, and desktop widths.
- Check for horizontal overflow on small screens.
- Use semantic HTML and accessible navigation.
- Verify keyboard accessibility for interactive elements.
- Describe any unresolved bugs honestly.
- Never report a test as passed unless it was executed.


# FlyRank Portfolio — AI Engineering Rules

## Rule 1: Preserve the existing architecture
Before generating code, inspect the relevant project files.
Use Next.js App Router, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS.
Do not introduce standalone HTML or JavaScript files
when the feature belongs in the Next.js application.

## Rule 2: Implement accessible forms
Every form input must have an associated label.
Validation errors must be visible and associated
with their fields using appropriate ARIA attributes.
Forms must support keyboard navigation and mobile screens.

## Rule 3: Verify before claiming completion
Run ESLint, TypeScript checks, and a production build.
Report the exact results.
Never claim that a feature works without verification.

## Rule 4: Avoid misleading submission behavior
A contact form without a configured email service
must clearly identify itself as a demo.
Never display a message claiming successful email
delivery when no email was sent.

## Rule 5: Protect project boundaries
Inspect Git status before making changes.
Avoid unrelated edits and do not commit secrets,
node_modules, or generated build files.
